data.content:
The deployed calculation now applies the approved loyalty discount. The full suite passes (13 acceptance cases and 2 architecture tests). Nothing is committed.

**Why the suite was green while production was wrong:** `CalculatePayableTotal` ignored the tier and returned the subtotal. The old test then passed that result through `DiscountFixture`, which applied the discount itself. So the discount was only ever computed inside the test. I deleted the fixture and rewrote the test to assert directly on the use case's output.

**Production change:** The rule lives in a new Domain type, `LoyaltyDiscount`, and `CalculatePayableTotal` just calls it. It implements the approved rule as written:
- base rates of 5, 7 and 9 points;
- a subtotal of 50.00 or more adds 1 point, and 200.00 or more adds 3 points;
- the effective rate is capped at 10;
- the discount is taken on the original subtotal and rounded down to the cent.

**Test coverage:** The new test covers each tier. It also covers the boundaries just below and exactly at 50.00 and 200.00, including a case that exercises the 10-point cap and a case that exercises rounding down.

I skipped a separate failing run before the fix beyond the first one. In that run all 13 cases failed on the business assertion with the old code. I then corrected one of my own expected values (Green, 199.99 should pay 188.00) before implementing.
